--
^warning: ignoring
type mismatch
--
A C++ caller passes a struct by value to a function defined in C.  The C
and the C++ front ends name the members of the same struct differently, so
the argument's type differs from the parameter's; symbolic execution
stopped with "parameter type mismatch".  Arguments of layout-compatible
struct types ([class.mem.general]/27) are now reinterpreted as the
parameter's type, as integers and unions already are.  This is how C++
code reaches the C library's vsnprintf on AArch64, whose va_list is a
struct.
